Z||000000||FieroTig||05-05-2001||11:07 AM||||My friend has been telling me about a car I should buy, he said that it was an 85 that had 86 GTP parts put on it.. there was a story behind it that went something like this... there was a 86 fiero fastback that pontiac had been working on makeing a gtp back in early 86. they gave it koni suspension, koni antisway bars and several other parts. it was put in storage in 87 and the project was nulled... the kid that got these parts was working for the storage company. he begged and begged for the parts when pontiac ordered the car be destroyed. pontiac wanted pictures before and after distruction, do the boss or whatever of the storage company said the kid could swap as many parts as possible with his 85 gt and that he would tell him the main parts he couldn't have. the parts that he was not allowed to take included an intake manifold which was chrome and had GTP ingraved in the center where the V6's normaly say Fiero, the rear quarter glass parts for they had GTP ingraved in them, the center caps to the custom 16 inch rims for they said fiero GTP. the parts that he was able to get without the forman knowing was the trunk cover that had GTP sown in, the glove thing on the pasenger side of the car which was the same. and the drivers side steering wheel has an emblum that looks simular to the fiero GT but instaed it says GTP. i am sorta interested in the car iether way, it needs to be finished but i was just trying to confirm or disfirm this story, oh, and if anybody asks i found the GTP parts in a crushed car at a salvage yard. the other thing that my friend tells me that gets me is that it has a sticker in the passenger window that says "GM Development Department" or something like that.. does anyone know anything about this car? and please don't get anyone in trouble about this.. i am just curious if it is true?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mach10||05-05-2001||12:56 PM||||Welcome to the forum!<P>In all of my research on this car, I've NEVER heard of something like this. If there are window stickers, then it sounds like someone did their own custom job. If by GTP, you mean the 3800-SII SC engine, GM never did anything like that for production. I guess it's possible, but I doubt it. GM had all of their prototypes under wraps at their R&D facilities, from what I gathered.<BR>From what you tell me, it sounds as if someone may have just tossed a 3800SC into a normal '86 GT, and decalled the snot out of it. <BR>Regardless, an almost finished Fiero w/ a 3800SC in it is well worth the effort. Go fer it!<BR>||||reg||6
Z||000002||FieroTig||05-05-2001||01:16 PM||||i don't know.. i will take pictures when i go look at it next weekend and post them. maybe that will help, i have no idea whats under the hood, i know that the car is sitting in pieces right now, sorta halfway done between a 85 gt to an 8g fastbakc body.. the guy might be full of it, infact i would bet on it, but my friend says that he thinks authentic.. i'll see what it is and send pics. maybe that will help. and by the way, this forum rocks. thanks for the welcome!||||reg||1
